   "text": {
    "L1": "Eating well is not about having the most food. It is about balance and variety.",
    "L2": "The myth says that more food always means better health. That is not true.",
    "L3": "A balanced diet has all nutrients, fibre and water in the right amounts for the body's needs.",
    "L4": "Rice and potato mainly give carbohydrates. Add dal or curd, vegetables or salad, fruit, and water.",
    "L5": "A long-term lack of one nutrient can cause a deficiency disease. These diseases are not caught from other people.",
    "L6": "For example, lack of iron can cause anaemia, and lack of vitamin C can cause scurvy.",
    "L7": "Millets such as ragi, jowar and bajra give fibre and minerals, need less water, and grow well in dry regions.",
    "L8": "Now choose the lunch that shows balance, variety and suitable amounts."
   },
